<h2>Segment 271 &mdash; seasonal sensations and their causes</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s271S"><span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s271r1">sos ka&#x27;i dus</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p2">su</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w3">zla ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w4">reg bya</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w5">cha shas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w6">gcig</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s271p7">gis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w8">nyer len</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p9">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w10">yi dvags</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p11">kyi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w12">las</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s271p13">kyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w14">lhan cig byed <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m15">rkyen</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w16">byas pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p17">la</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w18">brten</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s271p19">nas</span>, de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w20"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m21">lus</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m22">shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p23">kyi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w24">myong</span> byar gyur pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w25">tsha ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w26">reg bya</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w27">skye ba</span> dang , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s271r28">dgun dus</span> su <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w29">nyi ma</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w30">reg bya</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w31">cha shas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w32">gcig</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s271p33">gis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w34">nyer len</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p35">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w36">yi dvags</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p37">kyi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w38">las</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s271p39">kyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w40">lhan cig byed <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m41">rkyen</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w42">byas pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p43">la</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w44">brten</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s271p45">nas</span>, de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w46"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m47">lus</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m48">shes</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p49">kyi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w50">myong</span> byar gyur pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w51">grang ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w52">reg bya</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w53">skye ba</span> yod pa <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w54">lta bu</span> yin pa&#x27;i <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s271p55">phyir</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s271S">Another <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w54">example</span> would be the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w3">moon</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p2">in</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s271r1">springtime</span>; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w6">one</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w5">part</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w4">feel</span> of its rays on the body provides the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w8">material cause</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p9">and</span> then the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w12">karma</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p11">of</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w10">craving spirit</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w16">provides</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w14">contributing <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m15">factor</span></span>. <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w18">Based</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p17">on</span> these two, the spirit <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w27">gets</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w26">sensation</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w25">heat</span>, which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w24">experienced</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p23">by</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w20"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m22">consciousness</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m21">body</span></span>. So too with the <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s271r28">wintertime</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w29">sun</span>; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w32">one</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w31">part</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w30">feel</span> of its rays on the body provides the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w34">material cause</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p35">and</span> then the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w38">karma</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p37">of</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w36">craving spirit</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w42">provides</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w40">contributing <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m41">factor</span></span>. <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w44">Based</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p43">on</span> these two, the spirit <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w53">gets</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w52">sensation</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w51">cold</span>, which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w50">experienced</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p49">by</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s271w46"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m48">consciousness</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s271m47">body</span></span>.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p7"><span class="nul">Instrumental gis: no separate by/with exponent; the English presents the part as an active subject.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p13"><span class="nul">Instrumental kyis: karma is rendered as an active subject; no separate by/with word in this causal clause.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p19"><span class="nul">Conjunctive nas: the English Based-on clause supplies no separate after/from/then connective here.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p33"><span class="nul">Instrumental gis: the English presents this part as an active subject, without a separate by/with exponent.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p39"><span class="nul">Instrumental kyis: active karma-subject syntax has no separate by/with word here.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p45"><span class="nul">Conjunctive nas: no separate after/from/then connective follows the second Based-on clause.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s271p55"><span class="nul">Causal phyir: no separate because/for word occurs in this segment; the example explanation carries the connective relation.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, independent English-first original. The two seasonal expressions are phrases, not invented subword links. Each shared causal byas pa owns the provides after its karma owner; the other provides is left as a reprise. The two tactile-consciousness compounds retain body/consciousness members within their own occurrences. Six case/conjunction nulls and the closing causal null assert no separate lexical exponent; uncertain or distributed wording is omitted. GMR source text is unchanged.</div>
